# Development Workflow

## Environment Setup
- Use Python 3.12 or higher
- Create and activate a virtual environment for development
- Install dependencies from requirements.txt
- Set up environment variables from .env.template

## Version Control
- Create feature branches for new development
- Write meaningful commit messages
- Keep commits focused on single changes
- Squash multiple small commits before merging

## Code Review Process
- Review code for readability and maintainability
- Ensure adherence to project coding standards
- Check for security vulnerabilities
- Verify test coverage for new code

## Testing
- Write tests before implementing features (TDD approach)
- Run tests locally before committing
- Maintain high test coverage
- Include both unit and integration tests

## Documentation Updates
- Update README.md with any new features or changes
- Document all public APIs
- Include usage examples where helpful
- Keep documentation in sync with code changes

## Dependency Management
- Pin dependency versions in requirements.txt
- Regularly update dependencies for security patches
- Review new dependencies carefully
- Document the purpose of each dependency

## Quality Checks
- Run linters (flake8, pylint) to enforce coding standards
- Use type checking with mypy
- Format code with Black
- Sort imports with isort

## Performance Considerations
- Profile code to identify bottlenecks
- Optimize critical sections
- Consider memory usage and efficiency
- Document performance characteristics
